// A codata value indexed by parameters, with a computed observation.
//
// `Scaled` answers one observation, `doubled`. A *parameterized* copattern
// definition `def rec scaled(n) -> Scaled` is a codata value indexed by its
// parameter: it lowers to
//     thunk_ω { fn(n) { ret #{ doubled = thunk_ω (ret (n + n)) } } }
// -- a function returning the record-of-thunks carrier (ADR-66 §5.1's shape,
// minus the `fix self` binder that corecursion, wyrd-c2g4, would add).
//
// Note the observation body is a *computation* (`n + n`), delayed by the thunk:
// the work happens only when the observation is demanded, not when the codata
// value is built. This is the call-by-need laziness the negative half buys.
codata Scaled : Type {
  doubled : Integer;
}

def rec scaled(n: Integer) -> Scaled {
  .doubled => n + n
}

// `scaled(21)` applies the parameter, yielding the codata value; `.doubled`
// then observes it. The observation elaboration hoists the applied computation,
// so `scaled(21).doubled` is `let s <- scaled(21); force(RecordProj(s, doubled))`
// -- which forces the delayed `21 + 21`.
scaled(21).doubled

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: 42
